2026-04-22 | observation — heidegger-technical-upgrade-default | triggered by claim-heidegger-bcap-036 passage-review | [MIDDLE-FIELD RENAMED 2026-04-22 from `heidegger-technical-upgrade-pattern` to `heidegger-technical-upgrade-default` to match formal pattern-watch registration at item 066 (see registration entry below). This entry now serves as the 036 retrospective observation for the registered pattern.] Third consecutive accept of technical-upgrade on primary_heidegger material at the time of original logging (091 speaking→Discourse accepted as rich-preferred default; 079 speaking→Logos accepted per exegetical-context canonicalization; 036 visible→Disclosedness initially presented as Option A/B judgment, upgraded-on-passage-review to Option A accept after surrounding-passage evidence confirmed hermeneutic-disclosure reading). Pre-registration observation in canonical namespace; promoted to formal pattern-watch registration at item 066 when the pattern reached n=4 consecutive accepts.

2026-04-22 | pattern-watch — heidegger-technical-upgrade-default | triggered by claim-heidegger-bcap-066 (fourth consecutive accept) | thin English slugs denoting ordinary concepts that admit technical Heideggerian readings default to rich Heideggerian canonicals on primary_heidegger material when surrounding context establishes technical deployment. Observed instances (n=4 pre-populated via retrospective observation entries + 036 rename): 091 (speaking→Discourse), 079 (speaking→Logos), 036 (visible→Disclosedness, upgraded-on-review), 066 (essential→Essence). All four acceptances have been on BCAP; rule's scope for non-BCAP Heidegger untested. **Re-evaluation triggers (either fires forced evaluation):** (1) first GENUINE REJECTION of a technical-upgrade candidate on primary_heidegger material surfaces an edge case and forces scope refinement; (2) item-25 convention-validation checkpoint with accumulated data. **Genuine-rejection definition:** a case is a genuine rejection only if (a) on a primary_heidegger claim, (b) a thin English slug + rich Heideggerian canonical pair is available for the same concept, (c) the surrounding context establishes technical deployment, AND (d) the final label is nonetheless the thin slug. Cases where the thin slug is labeled because the surrounding context does NOT establish technical deployment are NOT rejections — they are correct applications of the rule's precondition (the rule's preconditions are not met, which is different from the rule being overruled on evidence). This distinction prevents the retrospective-ambiguity failure mode the §8.0 canonical-recipe discipline was designed to address. **Candidate §3.0 codification at re-evaluation:** "On primary_heidegger material, thin English slugs denoting ordinary concepts that admit technical Heideggerian readings default to the rich Heideggerian canonical when surrounding context establishes technical deployment; underreading is the failure mode, not overreading." **Scope question to resolve at codification:** whether the rule applies to all primary_heidegger material or specifically to Heidegger-on-Aristotle (BCAP-style) material — all four observed instances are from BCAP, so non-BCAP generalization is untested.

