2026-04-22 | observation — tri-form-synonymy-pattern-candidate | triggered by claim-papachristou-2013-127 (Soul / ψυχή / psyche) | first instance of three-way synonymy (rich English + rich Greek-glyph + thin transliteration) on a single concept; §3.0 rich-preferred-by-context-match corollary as written is silent on whether tri-form picks reduce to bi-form (collapse the thin slug, then choose between two rich) or require an explicit tri-form rule. Resolved here by collapsing thin first (eliminating psyche), then applying §3.0 between Soul and ψυχή with English-form preference per §3.2 — net pick: Soul. Worth tracking: if a second tri-form case surfaces and the right pick is non-obvious (e.g., context favors Greek-glyph over English-form, or thin transliteration is contextually correct against both rich forms), register pattern-watch with both instances and consider §3.2 row formalizing the tri-form procedure. Currently at n=1; do not register pattern-watch yet.

